/* Comic Vault v10.46: eight film dossiers and selected-film snapshots. */
window.ComicVaultMovieDetails1046={"version":"10.46","movies":{"halloween-1978-theatrical":{"title":"Halloween (1978)","overview":"A masked escapee brings terror to an ordinary Halloween night, while a babysitter protects two children and a psychiatrist searches for his former patient.","plot":["On Halloween night in 1963, six-year-old Michael Myers kills his sister Judith in their Haddonfield home. Fifteen years of confinement follow. When psychiatrist Sam Loomis and nurse Marion Chambers approach Smith’s Grove on October 30, 1978, they encounter patients wandering outside. Michael attacks their car and escapes. Loomis believes that the apparent absence of ordinary emotion in his patient conceals an immediate, lethal threat.","Back in Haddonfield, Laurie Strode delivers a key to the vacant Myers house as an errand for her father. Michael notices her and begins watching her movements. Laurie sees a masked figure near school and around the neighborhood, but the sightings disappear before she can make sense of them. Her friends Annie and Lynda are occupied with their own Halloween plans. Loomis arrives and persuades Sheriff Brackett to help search, while evidence around the old house reinforces his fears.","That evening, Laurie babysits Tommy Doyle while Annie watches Lindsey Wallace across the street. Annie brings Lindsey to Laurie so she can leave to meet her boyfriend, but Michael kills her before she departs. Lynda and Bob later enter the Wallace house and are also murdered. Unsettling telephone calls and the silence across the street eventually draw Laurie away from the children to investigate.","Laurie discovers the bodies and is attacked. She retreats to the Doyle house, where her priority becomes keeping Tommy and Lindsey alive. She resists Michael with nearby objects, hides, and sends the children to get help, but repeated defensive injuries do not stop him. Loomis finds the house and shoots Michael, who falls from the balcony. When the doctor looks down, the body is gone. Laurie survives without learning why she was targeted, and the ending leaves the familiar neighborhood haunted by a threat that has not been contained."],"spoiler":true,"continuity":"The original theatrical foundation. Laurie and Michael are not identified as siblings here; that revelation belongs to Halloween II. Later continuations must not be read backward into this account.","keyEvents":[{"title":"Escape","detail":"Michael returns to his hometown."},{"title":"Babysitting night","detail":"Laurie becomes responsible for Tommy and Lindsey."},{"title":"Unresolved threat","detail":"Michael disappears after Loomis shoots him."}],"locations":[{"name":"Haddonfield, Illinois","detail":"The fictional town."},{"name":"Myers house","detail":"Michael’s childhood home."},{"name":"Doyle and Wallace houses","detail":"The central neighborhood attacks."}],"connections":[{"title":"Next chapter","detail":"Halloween II continues the same night."}],"sources":[{"title":"Official Halloween film page","url":"https://halloweenmovies.com/films/halloween-1978/"},{"title":"AFI: Halloween (1978)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/moviedetails/56347"},{"title":"Film credits reference","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/moviedetails/56347"}],"cast":[{"name":"Laurie Strode","actor":"Jamie Lee Curtis","slug":"halloween-laurie-strode"},{"name":"Dr. Sam Loomis","actor":"Donald Pleasence","slug":"halloween-sam-loomis"},{"name":"The Shape","actor":"Nick Castle","slug":"halloween-michael-myers"},{"name":"Annie Brackett","actor":"Nancy Kyes (credited Nancy Loomis)","slug":"halloween-annie-brackett"},{"name":"Lynda van der Klok","actor":"P. J. Soles","slug":"halloween-lynda-van-der-klok"}],"triviaFilmId":"halloween-1978-theatrical","plotLabel":"Story and ending · spoilers","sourcePolicy":"Original synthesis of the existing source-scoped dossiers and official film reference. Theatrical plot; principal cast is a selection, not full credits.","castLabel":"Principal cast · selected roles","credits":{"releaseYear":1978,"director":"John Carpenter","screenplay":["John Carpenter","Debra Hill"],"edition":"Theatrical release"}},"halloween-ii-1981-theatrical":{"title":"Halloween II (1981)","overview":"The first film’s survivors enter a second ordeal as Michael follows Laurie into a hospital that should have offered safety.","plot":["The story resumes during the same Halloween night as the original film. Michael has disappeared after Loomis shoots him, leaving the doctor urgently searching Haddonfield. Laurie, injured and deeply shaken, is transported to Haddonfield Memorial Hospital. The institution offers treatment but little real security: the night staff is scattered, and the town’s search for the killer does not keep him from approaching his surviving victim.","In the streets, uncertainty produces another tragedy when a masked teenager is mistaken for Michael and is killed in a collision and fire. Brackett then learns that Annie is among the dead. Confronted with his daughter’s body, he blames Loomis and withdraws from the pursuit, which continues with Gary Hunt. The doctor’s warnings are no longer abstract, but identifying the killer in a town full of Halloween disguises remains dangerous.","At the hospital, Jimmy takes an interest in Laurie and tries to offer reassurance. Michael moves through the building, killing personnel and steadily removing the people who might protect her. Medication, injuries and disorientation limit Laurie’s ability to respond, yet she eventually leaves her room and struggles to evade him through the corridors and service areas. Jimmy’s attempts to help also leave him incapacitated; this account does not substitute the television version’s more reassuring ending.","Marion arrives with a marshal ordered to return Loomis to Smith’s Grove. Her disclosure that Laurie is Michael’s younger sister changes the direction of the search. Loomis insists on going to the hospital. There, Michael kills the marshal and wounds the doctor. Laurie shoots Michael in the eyes, and she and Loomis release medical gases. Loomis sends Laurie out and ignites the room. Michael emerges burning and collapses. Laurie is taken away alive, while the film leaves Loomis within the explosion and supplies no account of his later condition."],"spoiler":true,"continuity":"Continues October 31, 1978, despite its 1981 release. Shared predecessor of two separate branches: Halloween 4–6 and H20–Resurrection.","keyEvents":[{"title":"Hospital siege","detail":"Medical care cannot keep Michael away."},{"title":"Family revelation","detail":"Marion’s information redirects Loomis."},{"title":"Explosion","detail":"Laurie escapes the operating-room confrontation."}],"locations":[{"name":"Haddonfield Memorial Hospital","detail":"Principal setting."},{"name":"Haddonfield streets","detail":"Loomis and police search for Michael."}],"connections":[{"title":"Previous film","detail":"Immediately follows Halloween (1978)."},{"title":"Separate continuations","detail":"Halloween 4 and H20 take the story in different directions."}],"sources":[{"title":"Official Halloween film page","url":"https://halloweenmovies.com/films/halloween-ii-1981/"},{"title":"AFI: Halloween II (1981)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56628-HALLOWEEN-II"},{"title":"Film credits reference","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56628-HALLOWEEN-II"}],"cast":[{"name":"Laurie Strode","actor":"Jamie Lee Curtis","slug":"halloween-laurie-strode"},{"name":"Dr. Sam Loomis","actor":"Donald Pleasence","slug":"halloween-sam-loomis"},{"name":"Michael Myers","actor":"Dick Warlock","slug":"halloween-michael-myers"},{"name":"Jimmy","actor":"Lance Guest","slug":"halloween-jimmy"},{"name":"Marion Chambers","actor":"Nancy Stephens","slug":"halloween-marion-chambers"}],"triviaFilmId":"halloween-ii-1981-theatrical","plotLabel":"Story and ending · spoilers","sourcePolicy":"Original synthesis of the existing source-scoped dossiers and official film reference. Theatrical plot; principal cast is a selection, not full credits.","castLabel":"Principal cast · selected roles","credits":{"releaseYear":1981,"director":"Rick Rosenthal","screenplay":["John Carpenter","Debra Hill"],"edition":"Theatrical release"}},"halloween-iii-1982-theatrical":{"title":"Halloween III: Season of the Witch (1982)","overview":"A doctor and a grieving daughter investigate a mask company whose Halloween promotion conceals a mass-killing scheme.","plot":["A terrified Harry Grimbridge flees pursuers while clutching a Silver Shamrock Halloween mask. Taken to the hospital, he gives Dr. Daniel Challis a warning that makes little sense until an intruder murders him and destroys the getaway car in a fire. Harry’s daughter Ellie wants answers. The trail through her father’s business leads her and Challis to Santa Mira, where Silver Shamrock Novelties dominates both the local economy and the town’s atmosphere.","Posing as a married couple, the visitors stay at a motel and investigate the factory. The cheerful welcome from owner Conal Cochran contrasts with surveillance, curfews and disturbing incidents. Retailer Marge Guttman is gravely injured while examining a loose mask component. Enthusiastic salesman Buddy Kupfer and his family accept a factory invitation that seems like a reward for his success. Elsewhere, Teddy’s examination of the hospital attacker’s remains turns up mechanical evidence rather than the expected human body.","Challis discovers that Cochran’s operation combines android workers, a stolen Stonehenge fragment and devices hidden in the mask tags. A televised Halloween promotion will activate the devices while children are wearing the masks. The Kupfer family is used in a fatal demonstration. Cochran presents the planned sacrifice as the restoration of an ancient ritual, transforming a national advertising campaign into a delivery system for mass death.","After Ellie disappears and Challis is captured, he escapes and turns the tagged components and broadcast mechanism against the factory’s control center. He leaves with someone who appears to be Ellie, only to discover during an attack that she is mechanical. The film does not fully explain the original Ellie’s fate. Challis reaches a telephone and pleads for the commercial to be stopped. Two channels interrupt the transmission, but a third continues as he shouts for help. The ending withholds a final casualty count or confirmation that his own family is safe."],"spoiler":true,"continuity":"Standalone anthology continuity, not a Michael Myers sequel. Clips from Halloween on television are a film-within-a-film, not evidence that its characters share this story world.","keyEvents":[{"title":"Investigation","detail":"Ellie and Challis follow the mask connection."},{"title":"Factory revelation","detail":"The promotion conceals Cochran’s ritual."},{"title":"Broadcast crisis","detail":"Destroying the factory does not itself stop every transmission."}],"locations":[{"name":"Santa Mira, California","detail":"Company-controlled town."},{"name":"Silver Shamrock factory","detail":"The operation’s manufacturing and ritual center."}],"connections":[{"title":"Anthology entry","detail":"Independent of the Laurie/Michael branches."}],"sources":[{"title":"Official Halloween film page","url":"https://halloweenmovies.com/films/halloween-iii-1982/"},{"title":"AFI: Halloween III (1982)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56790-HALLOWEEN-IIISEASONOFTHEWITCH"},{"title":"Film credits reference","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/MovieDetails/56790"}],"cast":[{"name":"Dr. Daniel Challis","actor":"Tom Atkins","slug":"halloween-daniel-challis"},{"name":"Ellie Grimbridge","actor":"Stacey Nelkin","slug":"halloween-ellie-grimbridge"},{"name":"Conal Cochran","actor":"Dan O’Herlihy","slug":"halloween-conal-cochran"}],"triviaFilmId":"halloween-iii-1982-theatrical","plotLabel":"Story and ending · spoilers","sourcePolicy":"Original synthesis of the existing source-scoped dossiers and official film reference. Theatrical plot; principal cast is a selection, not full credits.","castLabel":"Principal cast · selected roles","credits":{"releaseYear":1982,"director":"Tommy Lee Wallace","screenplay":["Tommy Lee Wallace"],"edition":"Theatrical release"}},"halloween-iv-1988-theatrical":{"title":"Halloween 4: The Return of Michael Myers (1988)","overview":"Ten years after the hospital fire, Michael targets his young niece while her foster sister and Loomis try to protect her.","plot":["Ten years after the hospital explosion, Michael Myers remains in institutional care. During a transfer, he hears that Laurie Strode has died but left a daughter, Jamie Lloyd. He attacks the attendants and escapes toward Haddonfield. Loomis, scarred and walking with a cane, discovers the disaster and follows. Other officials are more willing than he is to believe that the missing patient cannot still be a threat.","Jamie lives with the Carruthers family and struggles with nightmares, grief and the knowledge of her connection to Michael. Her foster sister Rachel has teenage plans of her own but takes responsibility for Jamie’s Halloween. Their ordinary errands and trick-or-treating place them in a town that initially treats Michael’s return as rumor rather than an emergency. Loomis eventually convinces Sheriff Ben Meeker that Jamie is the target.","Michael’s attacks disrupt the town’s defenses and power supply. Armed residents organize their own search, adding the danger of panic and mistaken identification. Meeker tries to protect Jamie and Rachel at his home, where Kelly, Brady and Deputy Logan are also caught in the crisis. Michael penetrates the refuge, and Rachel must guide Jamie through a dangerous escape over the roof. The attempt to hide at the school offers only another temporary shelter.","Local men try to drive Rachel and Jamie to safety, but Michael reaches the vehicle and the pursuit continues. Rachel fights to protect Jamie, and police gunfire eventually drives Michael backward into a shaft. Jamie briefly approaches him before the confrontation ends. Back at the Carruthers home, the adults appear to have regained control, until Darlene’s scream is followed by the sight of Jamie with bloody scissors. Loomis reacts in horror and Meeker stops him from shooting her. The film closes on that disturbing image, not on an explanation that Jamie has permanently become another Michael."],"spoiler":true,"continuity":"Original-sequel branch after Halloween (1978) and Halloween II. Laurie is reported dead in this branch; H20’s living Laurie and son are a different continuation.","keyEvents":[{"title":"New target","detail":"Jamie becomes the focus of Michael’s return."},{"title":"Failed refuge","detail":"Meeker’s house is breached."},{"title":"Disturbing aftermath","detail":"Jamie’s behavior complicates the apparent ending."}],"locations":[{"name":"Haddonfield","detail":"Jamie’s home town."},{"name":"Meeker house","detail":"Attempted safe house."},{"name":"School and mine shaft","detail":"Final pursuit and confrontation."}],"connections":[{"title":"Next chapter","detail":"Halloween 5 follows Jamie’s aftermath."}],"sources":[{"title":"Official Halloween film page","url":"https://halloweenmovies.com/films/halloween-4-1988/"},{"title":"AFI: Halloween 4 (1988)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/58745-HALLOWEEN-4THERETURNOFMICHAELMYERS"},{"title":"Film credits reference","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/58745-HALLOWEEN-4THERETURNOFMICHAELMYERS"}],"cast":[{"name":"Jamie Lloyd","actor":"Danielle Harris","slug":"halloween-jamie-lloyd"},{"name":"Rachel Carruthers","actor":"Ellie Cornell","slug":"halloween-rachel-carruthers"},{"name":"Dr. Sam Loomis","actor":"Donald Pleasence","slug":"halloween-sam-loomis"},{"name":"Michael Myers","actor":"George P. Wilbur","slug":"halloween-michael-myers"},{"name":"Sheriff Ben Meeker","actor":"Beau Starr","slug":"halloween-ben-meeker"}],"triviaFilmId":"halloween-iv-1988-theatrical","plotLabel":"Story and ending · spoilers","sourcePolicy":"Original synthesis of the existing source-scoped dossiers and official film reference. Theatrical plot; principal cast is a selection, not full credits.","castLabel":"Principal cast · selected roles","credits":{"releaseYear":1988,"director":"Dwight H. Little","screenplay":["Alan B. McElroy"],"edition":"Theatrical release","story":["Dhani Lipsius","Larry Rattner","Benjamin Ruffner","Alan B. McElroy"]}},"halloween-v-1989-theatrical":{"title":"Halloween 5: The Revenge of Michael Myers (1989)","overview":"Jamie’s connection to Michael becomes central to a new pursuit as Loomis attempts to turn her insight into a trap.","plot":["Michael survives the gunfire and fall at the end of Halloween 4, escaping before the shaft is sealed. He reaches a hermit’s shelter and remains there until the following Halloween. When he rises again, he resumes his pursuit of Jamie. A mysterious man in black also arrives in Haddonfield, bearing the same strange mark associated with Michael. His identity and purpose are withheld.","Jamie is now at a children’s clinic after the traumatic events of the previous year. Initially unable to speak, she experiences a psychic connection that allows her to sense Michael’s actions. Loomis sees this link as a means of locating his former patient and presses Jamie for information. Rachel continues to care about her foster sister, but Michael kills Rachel early in the renewed attacks, leaving Jamie increasingly dependent on other adults and friends.","Tina and her friends prepare for a Halloween gathering at Tower Farm. Jamie tries to prevent harm, but warnings do not reliably reach the people at risk. Michael moves among costumes and familiar faces, kills members of the group and pursues Jamie and Billy. Tina intervenes to protect Jamie at the cost of her own life. The child’s connection to the killer gives her disturbing knowledge without giving her control over him.","Loomis and the police prepare a trap at the Myers house. Reports of trouble at the clinic draw officers away, and Jamie is exposed to Michael inside the building. She briefly appeals to him as her uncle, but the moment does not stop the attack. Loomis ultimately captures Michael with a net, tranquilizers and repeated blows, then collapses. Michael is taken to the police station to await transfer. An armed assault shatters that apparent victory: Jamie finds the station devastated and Michael gone. The film ends with her distress rather than a clear account of the attacker’s plan or the individual fate of every officer."],"spoiler":true,"continuity":"Continues Halloween 4 in the original-sequel branch. The Man in Black’s identity and later Thorn explanations are not established by this film alone.","keyEvents":[{"title":"Psychic link","detail":"Jamie senses Michael’s actions."},{"title":"Myers-house trap","detail":"Loomis’s tactics endanger the child he hopes to protect."},{"title":"Police-station attack","detail":"Michael’s capture does not resolve the threat."}],"locations":[{"name":"Children’s clinic","detail":"Jamie’s care setting."},{"name":"Tower Farm","detail":"Halloween gathering."},{"name":"Myers house and police station","detail":"Capture and final reversal."}],"connections":[{"title":"Next chapter","detail":"Halloween 6 develops the unresolved mystery."}],"sources":[{"title":"Official Halloween film page","url":"https://halloweenmovies.com/films/halloweenv-1989/"},{"title":"AFI Catalog: Halloween 5 (1989)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/moviedetails/58103"},{"title":"Film credits reference","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/moviedetails/58103"}],"cast":[{"name":"Jamie Lloyd","actor":"Danielle Harris","slug":"halloween-jamie-lloyd"},{"name":"Dr. Sam Loomis","actor":"Donald Pleasence","slug":"halloween-sam-loomis"},{"name":"Michael Myers","actor":"Don Shanks","slug":"halloween-michael-myers"},{"name":"Tina","actor":"Wendy Kaplan","slug":"halloween-tina"},{"name":"Rachel Carruthers","actor":"Ellie Cornell","slug":"halloween-rachel-carruthers"}],"triviaFilmId":"halloween-v-1989-theatrical","plotLabel":"Story and ending · spoilers","sourcePolicy":"Original synthesis of the existing source-scoped dossiers and official film reference. Theatrical plot; principal cast is a selection, not full credits.","castLabel":"Principal cast · selected roles","credits":{"releaseYear":1989,"director":"Dominique Othenin-Girard","screenplay":["Michael Jacobs","Dominique Othenin-Girard","Shem Bitterman"],"edition":"Theatrical release"}},"halloween-vi-1995-theatrical":{"title":"Halloween: The Curse of Michael Myers (1995)","overview":"Tommy Doyle and a retired Loomis confront a secret surrounding Michael while protecting Jamie’s baby and the family occupying the Myers house.","plot":["Six years after the attack on the police station, Jamie Lloyd is being held by a secretive group and gives birth to a son. Mary helps mother and child escape, then is killed by Michael. Jamie flees in a stolen vehicle and makes a desperate radio appeal. She hides the baby before Michael catches her. In the theatrical version, he kills her at the farm; the later hospital death shown in the Producer’s Cut is not part of this account.","Tommy Doyle, the child Laurie protected in 1978, is now an adult absorbed by the history of Michael Myers. He hears Jamie’s plea, follows the clues and finds the newborn, whom he calls Steven. Across from Tommy’s boarding house, Kara Strode lives with her son Danny and other relatives in the Myers house. Danny’s disturbing experiences and the family’s proximity to Michael’s old home draw them into the danger.","Loomis has retired, but the evidence of Jamie’s escape and recent childbirth brings him back. As Michael attacks the people around the Myers house, Tommy develops an explanation involving the Thorn symbol and an organization behind the killer. Kara discovers that Mrs. Blankenship is not the safe neighbor she appeared to be. Wynn, Loomis’s former colleague, is revealed as the Man in Black and becomes the link to the operation at Smith’s Grove.","Tommy and Loomis follow the abducted survivors to the institution. The theatrical climax emphasizes the medical facility and Michael’s violent attack on its personnel rather than presenting the Producer’s Cut’s ritual resolution. Tommy confronts Michael using injections and a pipe, giving Kara, Danny and Steven a chance to escape. Loomis helps them leave but remains behind. The final sounds do not show exactly what happens to him. Steven’s parentage, the group’s experiments and Thorn’s mechanisms should not be filled in by importing explicit claims from the alternate edition into gaps left by the theatrical cut."],"spoiler":true,"continuity":"Original-sequel branch: Halloween → Halloween II → Halloween 4 → Halloween 5 → this film. This dossier’s main plot follows the theatrical cut.","keyEvents":[{"title":"Jamie’s escape","detail":"Her hidden baby survives the pursuit."},{"title":"Wynn exposed","detail":"The institutional connection becomes explicit."},{"title":"Smith’s Grove","detail":"Tommy helps the survivors escape."}],"locations":[{"name":"Myers house","detail":"Occupied by Kara’s family."},{"name":"Boarding house","detail":"Tommy’s base."},{"name":"Smith’s Grove","detail":"Climactic confrontation."}],"connections":[{"title":"Edition warning","detail":"The Producer’s Cut changes Jamie’s fate sequence and the ending. Its ritual resolution and Loomis’s Thorn mark must remain separately labeled; neither is the theatrical ending."}],"sources":[{"title":"Official Halloween film page","url":"https://halloweenmovies.com/films/halloweenvi-1995/"},{"title":"Film credits reference","url":"https://www.miramax.com/movie/halloween-6-the-curse-of-michael-myers/"}],"cast":[{"name":"Tommy Doyle","actor":"Paul Rudd","slug":"halloween-tommy-doyle"},{"name":"Dr. Sam Loomis","actor":"Donald Pleasence","slug":"halloween-sam-loomis"},{"name":"Kara Strode","actor":"Marianne Hagan","slug":"halloween-kara-strode"},{"name":"Dr. Wynn","actor":"Mitchell Ryan","slug":"halloween-dr-wynn"},{"name":"Jamie Lloyd","actor":"J. C. Brandy","slug":"halloween-jamie-lloyd"},{"name":"Michael Myers","actor":"George P. Wilbur","slug":"halloween-michael-myers"}],"triviaFilmId":"halloween-vi-1995-theatrical","plotLabel":"Story and ending · spoilers","sourcePolicy":"Original synthesis of the existing source-scoped dossiers and official film reference. Theatrical plot; principal cast is a selection, not full credits.","castLabel":"Principal cast · selected roles","credits":{"releaseYear":1995,"director":"Joe Chappelle","screenplay":["Daniel Farrands"],"edition":"Theatrical release","note":"Release year verified by the official Halloween film page; the Miramax catalog’s 1994 metadata is not used."}},"halloween-h20-1998-theatrical":{"title":"Halloween H20: 20 Years Later (1998)","overview":"Laurie’s hidden life at a California boarding school collapses when Michael finds her twenty years after the original attacks.","plot":["Twenty years after the original Haddonfield attacks, Laurie Strode has built a hidden life under the name Keri Tate. She is the headmistress of Hillcrest Academy in California and the mother of seventeen-year-old John. Her fear of Michael has not ended: nightmares, alcohol and protective restrictions strain her relationship with her son. John wants independence, while Laurie struggles to believe that ordinary precautions could ever be enough.","In Illinois, Marion Chambers discovers a break-in connected to records about Laurie. Michael kills Marion and the nearby teenagers Jimmy and Tony, then continues his search. The stolen information leads him toward the identity Laurie has tried to keep separate from her past. Loomis is already dead in this branch; records and recreated narration recall him, but he does not return to intervene in the current attacks.","A school trip leaves the Hillcrest campus unusually empty. John, Molly, Charlie and Sarah stay behind for their own Halloween plans, while Laurie is with counselor Will Brennan and security guard Ronny remains nearby. Michael enters the campus and begins killing. The danger reaches John and Molly, and Laurie’s private terror becomes an immediate reality that the others can no longer dismiss. Confusion also causes Will to shoot Ronny before Michael kills Will; Ronny survives.","Laurie directs John and Molly to safety, then chooses to return and confront the man she has spent years fleeing. Their struggle moves through the school until Michael is apparently defeated. When authorities arrive, Laurie refuses to accept that the covered body means the danger is over. She takes the vehicle carrying it, drives away and crashes during a final struggle. The masked figure is trapped, reaches toward her, and Laurie beheads him with an axe. The 1998 film presents this as her decisive confrontation with Michael. Later reinterpretations are covered separately in the subsequent film’s dossier."],"spoiler":true,"continuity":"H20 branch after Halloween (1978) and Halloween II. Halloween 4–6, Jamie Lloyd’s story and Thorn are not part of this continuation.","keyEvents":[{"title":"Hidden identity","detail":"Keri Tate’s past catches up with her."},{"title":"School siege","detail":"The remaining students become targets."},{"title":"Confrontation","detail":"Laurie chooses to fight rather than continue hiding."}],"locations":[{"name":"Marion’s Illinois home","detail":"Opening attack."},{"name":"Hillcrest Academy, California","detail":"Laurie’s workplace and the central confrontation."}],"connections":[{"title":"Later continuation","detail":"Resurrection follows this branch; its revelations belong in that film’s dossier."}],"sources":[{"title":"Official Halloween film page","url":"https://halloweenmovies.com/films/halloween-h20-1998/"},{"title":"Film credits reference","url":"https://trancasfilms.com/film-halloween-h20-1998/"}],"cast":[{"name":"Laurie Strode / Keri Tate","actor":"Jamie Lee Curtis","slug":"halloween-laurie-strode"},{"name":"John Tate","actor":"Josh Hartnett","slug":"halloween-john-tate"},{"name":"Will Brennan","actor":"Adam Arkin","slug":"halloween-will-brennan"},{"name":"Molly Cartwell","actor":"Michelle Williams","slug":"halloween-molly-cartwell"},{"name":"Ronny Jones","actor":"LL Cool J","slug":"halloween-ronny-jones"},{"name":"Michael Myers","actor":"Chris Durand","slug":"halloween-michael-myers"}],"triviaFilmId":"halloween-h20-1998-theatrical","plotLabel":"Story and ending · spoilers","sourcePolicy":"Original synthesis of the existing source-scoped dossiers and official film reference. Theatrical plot; principal cast is a selection, not full credits.","castLabel":"Principal cast · selected roles","credits":{"releaseYear":1998,"director":"Steve Miner","screenplay":["Robert Zappia","Matt Greenberg"],"edition":"Theatrical release"}},"halloween-resurrection-2002-theatrical":{"title":"Halloween: Resurrection (2002)","overview":"A webcast staged inside Michael’s childhood home becomes a real survival ordeal for its participants and the viewers trying to help them.","plot":["The opening reinterprets H20’s ending: Michael crushed a paramedic’s throat and exchanged clothes with him, so Laurie killed the wrong man. Now institutionalized, Laurie has been waiting for Michael rather than simply withdrawing from the world. He enters the facility and kills guards Franklin and Willie. Laurie traps him on the roof but hesitates while trying to verify his identity, allowing him to stab her and send her falling. This ends her story in this continuation.","Back in Haddonfield, Freddie Harris and Nora are preparing DangerTainment, a live Internet investigation inside the Myers house. Six students are selected: Sara, Rudy, Jen, Bill, Donna and Jim. Sara is reluctant, but Freddie persuades her to participate. Cameras, planted props and a planned Michael impersonation make the event a mixture of staged scares and supposed investigation, creating confusion when the real Michael returns.","Michael kills cameraman Charley before the production understands what is happening. Inside the house, the students investigate rooms, debate the killer’s motives and discover signs that evidence has been manufactured. Bill and Donna are killed, while Freddie’s disguise briefly makes it seem that the entire threat is another trick. Jen’s genuine alarm is discounted because she has already performed for the cameras. As Michael attacks the remaining participants, the distinction between entertainment and emergency becomes unmistakable.","Sara’s online friend Myles, known to her as Deckard, watches from a party and recognizes that the murders are real. He alerts police and uses the camera feeds to send warnings and escape directions. Rudy tries to give Sara time to get away, but Michael kills him; Jim also dies. Sara discovers Nora’s body and continues fighting with improvised equipment. Freddie survives an attack and returns to help her escape the burning garage. Sara acknowledges Deckard’s assistance, and Freddie rejects further exploitation by the cameras. At the morgue, Michael opens his eyes, undermining the assumption that the fire finally ended the threat."],"spoiler":true,"continuity":"Continuation of the H20 branch, not Halloween 4–6. The paramedic switch is a revelation supplied by this film, not information established in H20’s on-screen story.","keyEvents":[{"title":"Laurie’s last stand","detail":"The opening closes her story in this branch."},{"title":"Webcast turns real","detail":"DangerTainment’s staged scares become actual attacks."},{"title":"Remote assistance","detail":"Myles helps Sara through the broadcast."}],"locations":[{"name":"Grace Andersen Sanitarium","detail":"Opening confrontation."},{"name":"Myers house, Haddonfield","detail":"Webcast and principal attacks."},{"name":"Morgue","detail":"Final reversal."}],"connections":[{"title":"Previous chapter","detail":"Follows H20, with a later reinterpretation of its ending."}],"sources":[{"title":"Official Halloween film page","url":"https://halloweenmovies.com/films/halloween-resurrection-2002/"},{"title":"Film credits reference","url":"https://halloweenmovies.com/films/halloween-resurrection-2002/halloween-resurrection-behind-the-scenes/"}],"cast":[{"name":"Sara Moyer","actor":"Bianca Kajlich","slug":"halloween-sara-moyer"},{"name":"Freddie Harris","actor":"Busta Rhymes","slug":"halloween-freddie-harris"},{"name":"Rudy","actor":"Sean Patrick Thomas","slug":"halloween-rudy-resurrection"},{"name":"Jen","actor":"Katee Sackhoff","slug":"halloween-jen-resurrection"},{"name":"Nora","actor":"Tyra Banks","slug":"halloween-nora-resurrection"},{"name":"Laurie Strode","actor":"Jamie Lee Curtis","slug":"halloween-laurie-strode"},{"name":"Michael Myers","actor":"Brad Loree","slug":"halloween-michael-myers"}],"triviaFilmId":"halloween-resurrection-2002-theatrical","plotLabel":"Story and ending · spoilers","sourcePolicy":"Original synthesis of the existing source-scoped dossiers and official film reference. Theatrical plot; principal cast is a selection, not full credits.","castLabel":"Principal cast · selected roles","credits":{"releaseYear":2002,"director":"Rick Rosenthal","screenplay":["Larry Brand","Sean Hood"],"edition":"Theatrical release","note":"Release year is 2002, not the 2001 production year shown in some catalog metadata."}}},"characterSnapshots":{"halloween-sam-loomis":{"halloween-ii-1981-theatrical":{"background":["Michael’s psychiatrist has just witnessed his patient survive gunfire and disappear. He continues the search rather than treating the earlier rescue as the end of the emergency."],"role":["Marion’s disclosure that Laurie is Michael’s sister sends Loomis back to the hospital. After being stabbed, he helps Laurie escape and ignites the medical gases with Michael still inside."],"status":"Last seen remaining in the room when it explodes. This film does not show his later condition.","relationships":[{"name":"Laurie Strode","detail":"Protects her during the hospital confrontation."},{"name":"Michael Myers","detail":"Former patient and the target of his pursuit."},{"name":"Marion Chambers","detail":"Supplies information that redirects his search."}],"sourceIds":["h2-afi"],"sources":[{"title":"AFI: Halloween II (1981)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56628-HALLOWEEN-II"}],"scope":"Halloween II (1981), theatrical story only. Background can include events established before this film, but no later continuations.","spoiler":true}},"halloween-laurie-strode":{"halloween-ii-1981-theatrical":{"background":["Laurie enters the hospital as an injured survivor of the earlier attacks, not as an experienced adult combatant. Treatment and medication leave her vulnerable."],"role":["She evades Michael through the hospital and takes an active role in the final defense, shooting his eyes and helping release gas before escaping. Jimmy offers support during the ordeal."],"status":"Survives and is taken away for further care.","relationships":[{"name":"Michael Myers","detail":"Revealed in this film to be her older brother."},{"name":"Dr. Sam Loomis","detail":"Helps her survive the final confrontation."},{"name":"Jimmy","detail":"Ambulance attendant who shows concern for her."}],"sourceIds":["h2-afi"],"sources":[{"title":"AFI: Halloween II (1981)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56628-HALLOWEEN-II"}],"scope":"Halloween II (1981), theatrical story only. Background can include events established before this film, but no later continuations.","spoiler":true}},"halloween-michael-myers":{"halloween-ii-1981-theatrical":{"background":["Michael continues the same night’s pursuit after surviving the confrontation at the Doyle house. The sequel reveals his family relationship to Laurie."],"role":["He follows Laurie to the hospital, attacks its staff and pursues her through the building. Laurie wounds his eyes; Loomis triggers the gas explosion."],"status":"Last shown engulfed in flames and collapsing. This snapshot does not import a later sequel’s survival explanation.","relationships":[{"name":"Laurie Strode","detail":"Younger sister and principal target."},{"name":"Dr. Sam Loomis","detail":"Pursuer who confronts him at the hospital."}],"sourceIds":["h2-afi"],"sources":[{"title":"AFI: Halloween II (1981)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56628-HALLOWEEN-II"}],"scope":"Halloween II (1981), theatrical story only. Background can include events established before this film, but no later continuations.","spoiler":true}},"halloween-leigh-brackett":{"halloween-ii-1981-theatrical":{"background":["Brackett continues the search as both sheriff and the father of Annie, whose death he has not yet learned about."],"role":["Seeing Annie’s body changes his role from active pursuit to personal grief. He blames Loomis and leaves the search; Gary Hunt continues with the doctor."],"status":"Alive; leaves the active investigation after identifying Annie.","relationships":[{"name":"Annie Brackett","detail":"His daughter, whose death he discovers."},{"name":"Dr. Sam Loomis","detail":"An increasingly painful and strained working relationship."},{"name":"Gary Hunt","detail":"Officer who continues the search."}],"sourceIds":["h2-afi"],"sources":[{"title":"AFI: Halloween II (1981)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56628-HALLOWEEN-II"}],"scope":"Halloween II (1981), theatrical story only. Background can include events established before this film, but no later continuations.","spoiler":true}},"halloween-marion-chambers":{"halloween-ii-1981-theatrical":{"background":["Marion has survived Michael’s escape and now accompanies the marshal sent to retrieve Loomis. Her institutional knowledge becomes crucial."],"role":["She tells Loomis that Laurie is Michael’s sister. At the hospital, she leaves to summon assistance while the crisis continues inside."],"status":"Survives the hospital crisis.","relationships":[{"name":"Dr. Sam Loomis","detail":"Colleague to whom she delivers the sealed family information."},{"name":"Laurie Strode","detail":"The subject of the information that redirects the rescue effort."}],"sourceIds":["h2-afi"],"sources":[{"title":"AFI: Halloween II (1981)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56628-HALLOWEEN-II"}],"scope":"Halloween II (1981), theatrical story only. Background can include events established before this film, but no later continuations.","spoiler":true}},"halloween-annie-brackett":{"halloween-ii-1981-theatrical":{"background":["Annie was killed earlier that night. This sequel’s brief appearance concerns the discovery of her body, not a recovery or a living return."],"role":["Her identification gives Brackett personal confirmation of the loss and causes him to withdraw from the pursuit. The reused portrait depicts her living appearance in the original film."],"status":"Deceased before the sequel’s new action; body-only appearance.","relationships":[{"name":"Sheriff Leigh Brackett","detail":"Her father identifies her body."},{"name":"Laurie Strode","detail":"Her surviving friend from the earlier events."}],"sourceIds":["h2-afi"],"sources":[{"title":"AFI: Halloween II (1981)","url":"https://catalog.afi.com/Film/56628-HALLOWEEN-II"}],"scope":"Halloween II (1981), theatrical story only. Background can include events established before this film, but no later continuations.","spoiler":true}}}};

